  "cause": "Piano-roll primary_pressed was paired with latest pointer.interact_pos. Press and later motion delivered in one frame therefore used a later position for initial note pitch/onset and target. The original log does not capture internal native frame boundaries, so exact per-gesture batching timing is not measured.",
  "baseline_regressions": {
    "unit": "piano_pencil_press_and_motion_in_one_frame_keep_the_press_origin failed: pressed pitch absent when press+motion arrived before one frame, release later.",
    "app": [
      "repeated_batched_pencil_drags_keep_the_pressed_onset_and_pitch failed: pressed pitch absent",
      "batched_movement_uses_the_note_under_press_and_keeps_its_length failed: expected start8, got2",
      "entering_the_canvas_after_an_outside_press_does_not_draw failed: inserted note64 at beat4"
    ],
    "logs": [
      "/workspace/scratch/rill-iteration-validation/round8-midi-press-unit-baseline.log",
      "/workspace/scratch/rill-iteration-validation/round8-midi-press-app-baseline.log"
    ]
  },
  "correction": "Capture primary press Event::PointerButton position and modifiers; use its position for initial keyboard focus, note/velocity target and gesture creation. Require fresh press origin inside canvas. Keep latest pointer for updates and release. Preserve existing enabled/modal/popup/current canvas layer guards.",
  "coordinate_space": "The piano roll uses untransformed egui screen-point rectangles, matching raw pointer event positions. No new coordinate transform or UI component is introduced.",
  "limits": [
    "The30.134-second extension is not automatically attributed to the onset bug; release endpoint snapping and initial note-length extension require separate evidence.",
    "Existing conservative behavior when latest pointer is outside canvas is retained; this is not universal cross-widget pointer capture.",
    "Multiple complete primary gestures within a single input frame are not newly supported.",
    "Round8 ratings precede this correction and must remain unchanged."
  ],
